1. Class
Definition: A class is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties (attributes) and behaviors (methods) of an object.
Real-time Example: Think of a Car. "Car" is a class because it defines common properties like color, brand, and speed, and actions like start() and stop().

2. Attributes
Definition: Attributes are the variables or properties of a class that store information about an object.
Real-time Example: For a Student class:
	•	Name = Rasool
	•	Roll Number = 101
	•	Branch = CSE-AI
Here, name, roll number, and branch are attributes.

3. Encapsulation
Definition: Encapsulation is the process of combining data and methods into a single class and restricting direct access to the data to protect it.
Real-time Example: An ATM machine hides your bank balance. You cannot directly access or change it. You can only use options like Withdraw, Deposit, or Check Balance after entering the correct PIN.

4. Polymorphism
Definition: Polymorphism means "many forms." The same method can perform different actions depending on the object.
Real-time Example: The Pay button in an online shopping app:
	•	Pay using UPI
	•	Pay using Credit Card
	•	Pay using Net Banking
The button is the same, but it performs different actions based on the selected payment method.

5. Inheritance
Definition: Inheritance allows one class (child) to acquire the properties and methods of another class (parent), promoting code reusability.
Real-time Example: A Smartphone inherits features from a Phone:
	•	Phone features: Calling, Messaging
	•	Smartphone adds: Camera, Internet, Apps
The smartphone reuses the phone's features and adds new ones.

6. Abstraction
Definition: Abstraction is the process of hiding complex implementation details and showing only the essential features to the user.
Real-time Example: When you drive a car, you only use the steering wheel, accelerator, brake, and gear. You don't need to know how the engine works internally. The complex details are hidden from you.


